(3) which u makes  1/2 c1 u^p = 1/4 (2N)^-2 ?   (c1 = (2N)^-2)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1/2 c1 u^p = 1/4 c1  <=>  u^p = 1/2  <=>  u* = 2^(-1/p)
  p    u* = 2^(-1/p)    u(1/48), N=2     u*/u(1/48)
  1         0.500000       2.604e-03      1.920e+02
  2         0.707107       2.604e-03      2.715e+02
  3         0.793701       2.604e-03      3.048e+02
  4         0.840896       2.604e-03      3.229e+02

  => the beta-FREE value 1/4(2N)^-2 is what 1/2 c1 u^p gives at u* = 0.5 (p=1) or
     0.707 (p=2) -- i.e. at u ~ O(1), the STRONG-coupling end u->1, NOT at beta<1/48
     where u = 2.6e-3 (N=2).  Hence 1/4(2N)^-2 is the u->1 (large-beta) evaluation
     of the same amplitude; at beta<1/48 the u^p form spuriously vanishes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(4) is a0 beta-free?  two spellings in the corpus, and what each implies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FOURWALL:81-86 : tube weight = a0 u^{4N_t}, a0 = (2N)^-2 [endpoint recouplings] [transverse sum]
                   -> the 4N_t plaquette activities are ALL in the exponent; the two
                      insertions' own measure sits at zeroth order (no extra c_f)
                   -> a0 = pure numbers, beta-FREE.
  AUDIT-COR:78   : a0(beta) = (2N)^-p [prod_{wall plaquettes} c_f] [recoupling]
                   -> would put the SAME c_f factors in a0 that u^{4N_t} already carries
                      (double count), and contradicts AUDIT-COR:87 (p=0).

  consequence if AUDIT-COR:78 were right: a0 ~ u^2 -> r0 -> 0 as beta -> 0,
  i.e. the beta->0 limit of the residue would be 0 at leading order.  Check at N=2:
    beta= 2.083e-02  u= 2.604e-03  a0~(2N)^-2 u^2 =    4.239e-07  vs a0=(2N)^-2 = 6.250e-02
    beta= 1.000e-03  u= 1.250e-04  a0~(2N)^-2 u^2 =    9.766e-10  vs a0=(2N)^-2 = 6.250e-02
    beta= 1.000e-05  u= 1.250e-06  a0~(2N)^-2 u^2 =    9.766e-14  vs a0=(2N)^-2 = 6.250e-02
  => the u^2 reading drives the amplitude to 0 with beta; Z05-AUDITI1:79's checked
     beta->0 behaviour (f1^2 -> a0 > 0, amplitude survives) selects the beta-FREE a0.

